      "result_tail": "'t safe for concurrent use either.\n- **Fix:** `internal/heartbeat/dedupe.go` now has a mutex-guarded `once(ctx, id, fn)`. The first caller for an id runs the save. Concurrent callers for the same id wait for it, then skip if it succeeded. `Handle` in `consumer.go` now calls this instead of `has`/`mark`.\n- **Failed saves:** A failed save is still not remembered, as before. A waiting caller then takes its own turn, so a failure can lead to another attempt rather than a silent drop. A waiter whose context ends returns that context's error.\n\nThe new test is `internal/heartbeat/concurrent_test.go`."
    },
