      "result_tail": "lone. The old `dedupe` made concurrent callers with the same id wait for the in-flight save. A failed save was not remembered, so a later caller retried. It also returned `ctx.Err()` if the context ended while waiting. A bare `FirstSeen` would return `nil` to the duplicate caller before the first save finished. If that save then failed, the heartbeat would be lost.\n\nSo I moved the old logic into the package as `Set.Once(ctx, id, fn) error`, and the consumer calls that. This keeps the consumer's behavior the same.\n\nI deleted `internal/heartbeat/dedupe.go` and added a small test for `FirstSeen`."
    },
